    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# Node Explainion\n \n## Counter Node: Cursor\n\nPagination Loop\nTwo words combined:\n\nPagination\nWhen a large set of data is split into smaller chunks (pages) instead of delivering everything at once. Just like how Google search results are split across multiple pages rather than showing 10 million results at once.\n\nLoop\nA process that repeats itself automatically until a condition is met.\n\nCombined = Pagination Loop\nA workflow/code that automatically keeps fetching the next page, over and over, until it has collected all the data it needs.\n\nExample for Twitter\nTwitter doesn't give you all tweets at once — it gives you 20 at a time\nEach batch comes with a cursor (a unique token like a bookmark) that says \"start from here next time\"\nSo the flow is:\n\nFetch tweets (no cursor)  →  gets tweets 1-20  +  cursor_A\nFetch tweets (cursor_A)   →  gets tweets 21-40 +  cursor_B\nFetch tweets (cursor_B)   →  gets tweets 41-60 +  cursor_C\n... and so on\nWithout the cursor, every single loop would just keep fetching the same first 20 tweets repeatedly. The cursor is what allows the workflow to \"turn the page\" and get fresh tweets each time.\n\n",
        "height": 928,
        "width": 768,
        "color": 3
      },
